<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Saturated Schnakenberg Turing wavelength for Dugesia japonica dorsal pigment at 6.912 µm (Holocene, Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 83.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 selects λ_c = 6.912 µm by solving D_u at diffusion ratio 48 for the saturated Schnakenberg Jacobian (κ = 0.15, a = 0.05, b = 1.40). Linear-mode growth matches analytic σ(k) at Pearson r = 0.99998 (RMSE 0.0054). Equal diffusion is stable (max σ = -0.565). The 16-frame, 640 px GIF paints that field through the segmented Nogi et al. 2009 plate. Not yet shown: the diffusion-ratio sweep, a KS comparison, the nonlinear peak wavelength, and the iNaturalist wild-type voucher. Overall 83.2/100 (faithfulness 81.3, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e4ebf5f02021c5cb9f6779addaebe15739877255; environment: python 3.12, lean not installed in this VM; theorems are Lean 4 prelude, unchecked here. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 80, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dugesia-japonica-turing-wavelength-s0.py at e4ebf5f02021c5cb9f6779addaebe15739877255, image/png, 552219 B, 1248×1104 px, artifact_sha256 a9ac178d5b9463acc6058929cc13b95e69c2cee26b43a039437342d3c76a9c73 (sha256 a9ac178d5b9463acc6058929cc13b95e69c2cee26b43a039437342d3c76a9c73), spec_fingerprint 69b07407b41111e3df409d09d284c8ed47d97c6e78075bf3f4f35e0a79d838da. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 69b07407b41111e3df409d09d284c8ed47d97c6e78075bf3f4f35e0a79d838da; artifact_sha256: a9ac178d5b9463acc6058929cc13b95e69c2cee26b43a039437342d3c76a9c73; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/dugesia_japonica_field_kalininsky_ccby4.jpg=e40acb76c9286a8d..., datasets/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/dugesia_japonica_ocellus_pigment_nogi2009.png=6abf2ae940aa3115..., datasets/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0/dugesia_japonica_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=2bc1220e0880d8c0...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the diffusion-driven instability and the critical wavenumber from the reaction Jacobian and the two diffusivities. | Schnakenberg (1979) gives the polynomial activator-substrate kinetics; Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) and Murray (1981) are the pigment-pattern reading. | Nogi, Zhang, Chan & Marchant (2009) published the CC BY 2.5 plate of regenerated Dugesia japonica with dorsal pigment and ocelli. | Orii, Ito & Watanabe (2002) describe extant Dugesia japonica anatomy. Herath & Lobo (2020) model planarian fission with Turing patterns, not this wavelength.; reconstructed_in_script: κ = 0.15 saturation, R = D_v/D_u = 48, and D_u solved so λ_c = 6.912 µm on a 48.384 µm patch (seven linear wavelengths). | Spectral diffusion plus explicit reaction, seed 3213, and the linear-mode Pearson comparison. | Body mask and ocellus cups segmented from the Nogi plate and used as the display domain.; transfer_boundary: Fish pigment waves (Kondo 2009) and Schmidtea eye regeneration (Lapan & Reddien 2012) are not measurements of a 6.912 µm Dugesia japonica mode. | The Nogi plate is a praziquantel-regeneration micrograph without a scale bar. Pixel size is not 6.912 µm.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that 6.912 µm was measured on Dugesia japonica in any of the cited papers. It is this slot's detail-scale operating point. | Does not claim a fossil predecessor. The chronoseries is Holocene 1/1, age 0 Ma. | Does not claim the rendered body outlines are a pixel-perfect copy of four separate worms; the brightness mask merges some animals.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Report the nonlinear steady-state dominant wavelength next to the linear λ_c = 6.912 µm. The saturated field shifts off the linear mode.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add a two-sample KS (or equivalent) comparison of the specimen interior histogram and the simulated interior, with the statistic not equal to its reference.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Draw the diffusion-ratio sweep and the equal-diffusion ablation on the comparison figure. They are computed and not shown.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Segment the CC BY 4.0 iNaturalist wild-type voucher and record a body metric that is not copied from the Nogi plate.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.32e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

